0..75 Comment "// A natural literal read through a reader, in a body and as a definition\'s"
76..89 Comment "// own value."
90..92 Comment "//"
93..165 Comment "// A literal at a type a `FromNat` model carries is the reader\'s call. A"
166..240 Comment "// function\'s body runs that call, so the literal there settles to a leaf."
241..243 Comment "//"
244..316 Comment "// A definition\'s own value has no computation around it to run the call"
317..391 Comment "// before. The reader\'s call is pure, so the value stands as what the call"
392..450 Comment "// returns, and each read of the definition runs the call."
451..453 Comment "//"
454..514 Comment "// - see: #4806 — the refusal at the literal, before #4812"
515..581 Comment "// - see: #4812 — a definition\'s own value that runs a pure call"
582..662 Comment "// - see: `ledger/features/literal-reading.gandr` — the literals readers carry"
